<%#
  The help panel. On by default, switched off in the settings.

  Every page passes a translation key prefix; the panel renders the purpose of
  the page and a short list of what can be done on it. The texts live in the
  locale files, never here — that is what makes them translatable and what keeps
  a second language from drifting behind the first.

  Two ways to make it go away, and they answer different questions. "Close" is
  for right now, on this page, because the box is in the way of what the
  operator is doing; it comes back next time. The setting is for somebody who
  has read them and does not want them any more. Offering only the second one
  makes a person turn off all the help to get past one box.
%>
<% if help_mode? %>
  <aside class="help" data-controller="dismissable">
    <h2><%= t("help.title") %></h2>
    <p><%= t("#{key}.purpose") %></p>

    <% steps = t("#{key}.steps", default: []) %>
    <% if steps.present? %>
      <ul>
        <% steps.each do |step| %><li><%= step %></li><% end %>
      </ul>
    <% end %>

    <p class="muted">
      <%= t("help.switch_off_hint") %>
      <button type="button" class="as-link" data-action="dismissable#dismiss"><%= t("help.close") %></button>
    </p>
  </aside>
<% end %>
